  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fa9cf094-f106-4cca-abaa-eb938d76a6c2-image.png\" style=\"width: 232px; height: 156px;\" /><br />In the above circuit is we are applying high voltage in any one of the diodes or in both diodes simultaneously&nbsp;then we get a high out due to forward biasing of diode while we are applied low voltage in both the diode then we get low voltage so this is like OR gate.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/807b9505-21fc-4a56-9268-f3e59f252d57-image.png\" style=\"width: 321px; height: 278px;\" /></p><p>In the above circuit which is an NPN transistor in a common emitter configuration having a phase difference of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;between input voltage and output voltage, when we are applied high voltage then we get low voltage vice-versa so,&nbsp;the circuit is the same as NOT gate.</p>",
